{"ts": "2026-10-16T12:51:24.505668Z", "run_id": "r-20261016T1216Z-4b11", "unit": "openspec:add-telemetry-runtime", "seq": 55, "type": "task.red_ok", "task": "4.4", "base": "db546034bb15700933aa6cc78dac879f69b0de82", "tests": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_logger_level::test_otlp_exporter_logger_is_critical_while_running_and_restored_after_shutdown", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_logger_level::test_otlp_exporter_logger_level_round_trips_across_two_init_shutdown_cycles"], "frozen": [], "notes": "C-1d2bd9a4 is already satisfied at HEAD by 7ceb3e1: _mute_exporter_logger saves the exporter logger level when none is saved and sets CRITICAL, and _restore_exporter_logger (called from _teardown, hence shutdown_telemetry and reset_telemetry) restores it. No production change, no stub, no suppression. The two new tests drive the one teardown seam through init/shutdown and init/shutdown again against a real OTLP/HTTP endpoint nobody listens on. Because the behaviour exists the criterion is pre-satisfied and the harness must confirm it: its Python zero-value run zeroes telemetry.traced (a public function used as a decorator at import in storage.py), aborting collection, so I made the base-run confirmation deterministic. The test module defines its own autouse _reset_telemetry fixture that shadows the root conftest.py fixture of the same name for this module only and tolerates the helper being absent; against the unit base (telemetry.py and config.py swapped, root conftest.py kept) both tests run and FAIL BY ASSERTION (assert 0 == 50: the base builds no OTLP exporter and never mutes the logger). I verified this with a full-suite base simulation (2 failed assertions; the rest errors because the base lacks reset_telemetry). Against HEAD both pass and the full suite is green (1630 passed, 114 skipped, coverage 90.80%). The module fixture changes no existing test and not conftest.py. Accepted findings: F-1619b9 (one WARNING per bad shared variable; OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_PROTOCOL checked once) is task 4.1 and untouched; F-0ad188 (_Scrubbing keeps _inner) is 4b.2/7.1 and untouched; F-fea82d (comma lists; helper signatures) is 3/4/6 and untouched; F-5d64eb (unstated failure cases) and F-f4dc92 (bounded-exit Event, subprocess env, spans() tuple meaning) are 3/5/1.2 and untouched. No Open questions; no product decision.", "criteria": {"C-1d2bd9a4": {"tests": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_logger_level::test_otlp_exporter_logger_is_critical_while_running_and_restored_after_shutdown", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_logger_level::test_otlp_exporter_logger_level_round_trips_across_two_init_shutdown_cycles"], "proof": "pre_satisfied", "discriminating": ["packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_logger_level::test_otlp_exporter_logger_is_critical_while_running_and_restored_after_shutdown", "packages.core.tests.test_telemetry_logger_level::test_otlp_exporter_logger_level_round_trips_across_two_init_shutdown_cycles"], "via": "base_run", "base_sha": "7942c5591c0bcd29f2f50fabefeea04ea99fe9f9"}}, "suppressions": [], "tdd": "already-satisfied"}
